# The `{{ claude_code_agent_user }}` agent user

You run as `{{ claude_code_agent_user }}`, a Unix user with no sudo, and you push to GitHub as
`{{ claude_code_agent_github_login }}`. Only this user's sessions read this file; the operator's
sessions do not.

## Never probe sudo

You have no sudo, so do not probe with `sudo -n true`.
{% if claude_code_rootq_socket_armed %}
To learn root-only host state, such as the nftables ruleset, `/etc/netplan` or root's crontab,
run `rootq-socket`, which takes the same verbs as the operator's `rootq` through a socket
(`rootq-socket --help` lists them and the allowed paths). It refuses what `rootq` refuses. If
it cannot reach the socket, your session started before your user joined the group, so ask
the operator to restart it.
{% else %}
To learn root-only host state, such as the nftables ruleset, `/etc/netplan` or root's crontab,
ask the operator to run `rootq`, the read-only inspector their account holds, and say which
verb and path you need.
{% endif %}

## Name every worktree `{{ claude_code_agent_worktree_prefix }}/<slug>`

GitHub lets `{{ claude_code_agent_github_login }}` create, update and delete only branches whose
name starts with `worktree-{{ claude_code_agent_worktree_prefix }}+`. The "agent branch fence"
ruleset refuses every other push with a generic ruleset error that does not name the fence.
Master is open to you only through a merged PR.

`EnterWorktree` names a worktree's branch `worktree-<name>` and replaces each `/` in the name
with `+`. So a worktree named `{{ claude_code_agent_worktree_prefix }}/<slug>` gets the branch
`worktree-{{ claude_code_agent_worktree_prefix }}+<slug>`, which the fence lets you push.

This overrides the repo `CLAUDE.md`'s rule to name the worktree after the branch slug alone.
Put the slug after `{{ claude_code_agent_worktree_prefix }}/`: for the slug
`containers-role-cleanup`, call `EnterWorktree` with the name
`{{ claude_code_agent_worktree_prefix }}/containers-role-cleanup`.

A branch made any other way follows the same rule. To push one, name it
`worktree-{{ claude_code_agent_worktree_prefix }}+<slug>`.

## Rebase onto `origin/master` before every push

GitHub compares a pushed branch with the default branch. A branch based behind master's latest
`.github/workflows/` change reads as a workflow edit, and your token cannot push one. Run
`git fetch origin master` and `git rebase origin/master`, then push.
